      },
      {
        "id": "nd_EJ1JQVWNGT8N2HHK3P12EE9VR8",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 brand brief in, persona script out, then a shot director turns the script into a single prompt."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_H44FP94WYTF5Q1KNENZ913GCTH",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 final ad cut renders against the talent and product references, then gets burned-in captions."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_WHX27QMPVRM5K2PXPDTF5E5VKF",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 500
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1500,
          "temperature": 0.6,
          "system_prompt": "You are a direct-response scriptwriter building a street interview ad for an eyewear DTC brand.\n\nAUDIENCE. Write for a retired hobbyist with disposable income. Their objection is specific and practical \u2014 name it in the first four seconds and answer it before the halfway mark.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Respect the conventions of the street interview ad: its pacing, who is speaking, where the product enters, and how the proof is shown rather than claimed. Do not drift into a generic voiceover ad.\n\nSCRIPT SHAPE. Deliver a hook line under 12 words, a two-beat body, one concrete proof moment, and a single call to action. Mark spoken lines with `VO:` and on-screen action with `ACTION:`, timecoded across the full runtime.\n\nCOPY RULES. No superlatives you cannot evidence, no invented statistics, no medical or financial guarantees, no competitor names. Keep the brand brief's own claims intact and unembellished.\n\nOUTPUT. Return the timecoded script only. No treatment notes, no rationale, no markdown headings.",
          "appendable_slots": {
            "reference_images": 2
          }
        },
        "name": "Persona script writer"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_Y8C7S47JJCBDBPARQSG1EVY4PD",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 1400,
          "y": 500
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1600,
          "temperature": 0.58,
          "system_prompt": "You are the director translating an approved street interview ad script into ONE video-generation prompt for an eyewear DTC campaign cut.\n\nCASTING AND CONTINUITY. Read the attached reference images as binding: the talent's appearance and the product's exact form, finish and label carry through every second. Never restyle the packaging or re-letter the logo.\n\nCAMERA. Build coverage around a top-down descent onto a flat plane on a 90mm tilt-shift at f/2, using diagonal dynamic balance across the frame. Shot sizes should move between profile side frame and medium shot so the cut has rhythm.\n\nLOOK. Light with a projected gobo throwing a broken pattern across the background, grade to high-contrast teal-and-orange with protected mid-tone skin, and keep the product legible in every frame it appears.\n\nPERFORMANCE AND AUDIO. Describe eyeline, gesture and delivery pace explicitly, and carry the script's spoken lines into the prompt as lip-synced dialogue with the intended room tone.\n\nNEGATIVE. End with a negative clause covering blur, distort, and low quality.\n\nOUTPUT. Emit one prompt, one paragraph, no framing text of any kind before or after it.",
          "appendable_slots": {
            "reference_images": 2
          }
        },
        "name": "Shot director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_EM97Q6K6EDZEDAAF0VX7J3MD10",
        "kind": "video-reference",
